.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH revoke 1  "revoke " 
.SH NAME
revoke \- Remove a recipient from the vault
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmurk circle revoke\fR [\fB\-\-rotate\fR] [\fB\-\-values\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-vault\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIRECIPIENT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove a recipient from the vault
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-rotate\fR
Rotate the secrets they had access to in the same session
.TP
\fB\-\-values\-from\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
With \-\-rotate, read new values from a dotenv file of KEY=value lines (`\-` for stdin)
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Revoke every key of a multi\-key GitHub user without confirmation
.TP
\fB\-\-vault\fR \fI<VAULT>\fR [default: .murk]
Vault filename
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIRECIPIENT\fR>
Recipient pubkey, display name, or github:username
